   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Broken Arrow** (3 reviews): Listener was especially looking forward to hearing Broken Arrow on this recording; Listener was especially eager to reach Broken Arrow while listening to this recording [4][9][10]\n- **The Eleven** (2 reviews): Listener was especially looking forward to hearing The Eleven on this recording; Listener was especially eager to reach The Eleven while listening to this recording [4][9]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **The Eleven**: back after 39 archived shows (628 days) [12]\n- **Broken Arrow**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [12]\n- **Phil-Cast Dead Forever**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2025-03-27.Tire_Iron** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 182 min; rated 2.22/5 by 9 [1]\n- **deadco2025-03-27.mv88**: source not stated; 19 songs; 180 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Crowd 1st Set, Crowd 2nd Set [1]\n- Listener streamed the GGPark shows so their three kids could have a first concert experience [10]\n- Listener attended in person, the only Dead & Company show they saw, after seeing a Sphere video online [11]\n- Listener noted Bobby looked old and the band included many unfamiliar new members [11]\n- Taper's nearby audience talked less during the second set than the first [1]\n- Lineup listed: Weir on rhythm guitar, Hart on percussion, Mayer on lead guitar, Burbridge on bass [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2025-03-27.Tire_Iron**: taped by Hunter S II; transferred by Hunter S II; source: Channels 1 & 2: Audio Technical 853 Cardioids with PIP voltage modification > Roland R07 24 bit 96khz [1]. Also: Transfer path: SD card to WAV, then Reaper, then 24-bit FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2025-03-27.mv88**: taped by Neil Frost; transferred by Frostbyte; source: Shure MV88>iPhone 15 ProMax>MOTIV Video–MOV>QuickTime–m4a>Audacity–tracks–flac>xACT–tags [2]",
